{"id": "EUVD-2026-102289", "enisaUuid": "1943962c-8ceb-3a5a-ad32-edfd067cc4b4", "description": "WildMIDI through 0.5.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the HMP parser _WM_ParseNewHmp() that allows attackers to read beyond buffers via underflowed chunk lengths. Attackers can supply a crafted .hmp file with a chunk length of 0-12 that wraps to roughly 4 GB, crashing applications or exposing heap bytes through WildMidi_GetInfo().", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:09:53", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/wildmidi-hmp-chunk-length-underflow-oob-read", "https://github.com/Mindwerks/wildmidi/blob/340472ed4633d139d30c660b90eca03c1320e593/src/f_hmp.c#L258-L261", "https://github.com/Mindwerks/wildmidi/blob/340472ed4633d139d30c660b90eca03c1320e593/src/internal_midi.c#L2166-L2172", "https://github.com/Mindwerks/wildmidi", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wildmidi-through-0.5.0-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-wm-parsenewhmp"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pgxh-r3r9-7phj", "CVE-2026-111162"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c50a7284-a8e7-3501-8519-a7c2c9695c3d", "product": {"name": "WildMIDI", "vendor": {"name": "Mindwerks"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "552d976f-3ce8-392d-a389-ee3b920ac498", "vendor": {"name": "Mindwerks"}}], "isExploited": false}